            <div xml:id="d396">

                <pb facs="0423" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg415"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/14327: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-08-25T21:00:00+03:25">August 25, 1941—9 p.m. [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">a.m.</hi>]</date><lb/>[Received August 25—4
                        p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>104. The British note mentioned in my No. 103<anchor n="89" xml:id="d396-f1"/>
                    and a similar note from the Russian Government were delivered to the Prime
                    Minister at 4 a.m. today. The hour of delivery was advanced in view of the
                    instructions of the Soviet Ambassador to deliver his note without delay.</p>
                <p>The Shah has asked to see the Russian and British Envoys at [apparent omission]
                    a.m. this morning. I shall report the results of their conversation immediately
                    thereafter.</p>
                <p>All is quiet in Tehran this morning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
